          "The test is the same for all four, and it has six parts: does the shop hold the stock it lists, can it prove a sealed box is sealed, does it state the full landed cost before checkout, does it handle customs paperwork honestly, does it answer when something goes wrong, and does it sell at a price that makes sense once all of that is counted. A shop failing any one of those is not the cheapest option — it is the most expensive lesson in the hobby, priced as a bargain. The sections below run each check with numbers from our shelf. Our guide to [buying TCG from Japan](/blog/buying-tcg-from-japan-shipping-customs-proxy/) prices the three main routes side by side; this guide is the checklist you run against whichever route you choose."
